    skos:prefLabel "3 Enterprise Agreement"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-2-sec-3 ;
    values:originalText "(1) The Department of Health and Aged Care Enterprise Agreement: (a) continues, at and from the transition time, to cover and apply to APS employees: (i) who it covered and applied to immediately before the transition time; and (ii) who, at the transition time, are members of the staff of the Australian Centre for Disease Control; and (b) covers and applies to APS employees who are at the classification levels covered by the Department of Health and Aged Care Enterprise Agreement whose employment as a member of the staff of the Australian Centre for Disease Control commences at or after the transition time. (2) At and after the transition time, the Department of Health and Aged Care Enterprise Agreement covers and applies to the Director-General of the CDC as the Agency Head of the APS employees who are members of the staff of the Australian Centre for Disease Control. (3) This item does not prevent the variation or termination of the Department of Health and Aged Care Enterprise Agreement in accordance with law. (4) This item does not prevent the terms and conditions of employment of APS employees who are members of the staff of the Australian Centre for Disease Control from being varied at or after the transition time: (a) in accordance with those terms and conditions; or (b) by or under a law. (5) This item does not affect the operation of section 58 of the Fair Work Act 2009. Note: Section 58 of that Act deals with the interaction between one or more enterprise agreements." ;
    skos:definition "(1) The Department of Health and Aged Care Enterprise Agreement: (a) continues, at and from the transition time, to cover and apply to APS employees: (i) who it covered and applied to immediately before the transition time; and (ii) who, at the transition time, are members of the staff of the Australian Centre for Disease Control; and (b) covers and applies to APS employees who are at the classification levels covered by the Department of Health and Aged Care Enterprise Agreement whose employment as a member of the staff of the Australian Centre for Disease Control commences at or after the transition time. (2) At and after the transition time, the Department of Health and Aged Care Enterprise Agreement covers and applies to the Director-General of the CDC as the Agency Head of the APS employees who are members of the staff of the Australian Centre for Disease Control. (3) This item does not prevent the variation or termination of the Department of Health and Aged Care Enterprise Agreement in accordance with law. (4) This item does not prevent the terms and conditions of employment of APS employees who are members of the staff of the Australian Centre for Disease Control from being varied at or after the transition time: (a) in accordance with those terms and conditions; or (b) by or under a law. (5) This item does not affect the operation of section 58 of the Fair Work Act 2009. Note: Section 58 of that Act deals with the interaction between one or more enterprise agreements."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "8ed4ccb70ca316d2b1e88f1131ad1ccef20ef958a583441ac36329ba472d828c" ;
    cof:pageNumber "33"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Continues and applies to APS employees, including those at the Australian Centre for Disease Control." ;
