doc:sch-2-sec-5 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "5 Transitional rules" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "(1) The Health Minister may, by legislative instrument, make rules prescribing matters: (a) required or permitted by this Act to be prescribed by the rules; or (b) necessary or convenient to be prescribed for carrying out or giving effect to this Act. (2) Without limiting subitem (1), the rules may prescribe matters of a transitional nature (including prescribing any saving or application provisions) relating to: (a) the amendments or repeals made by this Act; or (b) the enactment of the Australian Centre for Disease Control Act 2025. (3) Without limiting subitem (2), rules made for the purposes of that subitem before the end of the period of 12 months starting at the transition time may modify the operation of the provisions of this Act or the Australian Centre for Disease Control Act 2025 or any other Act or instrument. (4) To avoid doubt, the rules may not do the following: (a) create an offence or civil penalty; (b) provide powers of: (i) arrest or detention; or (ii) entry, search or seizure; (c) impose a tax; (d) set an amount to be appropriated from the Consolidated Revenue Fund;  Application, saving and transitional provisions  Schedule 2 General provisions  Part 1 No. 62, 2025 Australian Centre for Disease Control (Consequential Amendments and Transitional Provisions) Act 2025 (e) directly amend the text of this Act or the Australian Centre for Disease Control Act 2025. (5) This Schedule (other than subitem (4)) does not limit the rules that may be made for the purposes of subitem (1).  Schedule 2  Application, saving and transitional provisions" ;
    cof:pageNumber "34"^^xsd:integer .

concept:c2025a00062-sch-2-sec-6 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "6 Things done by, or in relation to, the Commonwealth Chief"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-2-sec-6 ;
    values:originalText "Medical Officer (1) If, before the transition time, a thing was done by, or in relation to, the Commonwealth Chief Medical Officer, in the capacity of the Director of Human Biosecurity, for the purposes of: (a) the old Biosecurity Act; or (b) a legislative instrument made under the old Biosecurity Act; then the thing has effect, at and after the transition time, as if it had been done by, or in relation to, the Health Secretary in the capacity of the Director of Human Biosecurity. (2) Subitem (1) does not apply in relation to a determination made under subsection 42(1) of the old Biosecurity Act. (3) The transitional rules may provide that subitem (1) does not apply in relation to a specified thing done by, or in relation to, the Commonwealth Chief Medical Officer, in the capacity of the Director of Human Biosecurity." ;
    skos:definition "Medical Officer (1) If, before the transition time, a thing was done by, or in relation to, the Commonwealth Chief Medical Officer, in the capacity of the Director of Human Biosecurity, for the purposes of: (a) the old Biosecurity Act; or (b) a legislative instrument made under the old Biosecurity Act; then the thing has effect, at and after the transition time, as if it had been done by, or in relation to, the Health Secretary in the capacity of the Director of Human Biosecurity. (2) Subitem (1) does not apply in relation to a determination made under subsection 42(1) of the old Biosecurity Act. (3) The transitional rules may provide that subitem (1) does not apply in relation to a specified thing done by, or in relation to, the Commonwealth Chief Medical Officer, in the capacity of the Director of Human Biosecurity."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "b40b0e28cf1880fbbd00a6633c763e730651aeefb359eb091e56ccca059e5ade" ;
    cof:pageNumber "36"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Things done by, or in relation to, the Commonwealth Chief Medical Officer have effect as if done by the Health Secretary." ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <c2025a00062.pdf> ;
    dc:source "c2025a00062.pdf, p.36" ;
